Subject: Use fork() instead of vfork() in dash job control under Fil-C
Policy-Class: P2-Package
Rationale: Fil-C requires capability-safe process creation via fork() rather than shared-stack vfork().
Upstream-Status: Fil-C-Specific
Fil-C-Origin-Commits: cede3de0

diff --git a/src/jobs.c b/src/jobs.c
--- a/src/jobs.c
+++ b/src/jobs.c
@@ -999,7 +999,7 @@
 		mypid = getpid();
 	vforked = mypid;
 
-	pid = vfork();
+	pid = fork();
 
 	if (!pid) {
 		forkchild(jp, n, FORK_FG);
